Important distinction
Maximum − allocated can be reclaimed immediately by lowering the maximum. No data work needed.
Allocated − used requires shrinking the data files first (DBCC SHRINKFILE), which is slower, can fragment indexes, and should be scheduled. Treat it as a separate, later task.
Always leave headroom — set the new maximum at allocated plus 20–30%, never at allocated exactly, or the database will fill and stop accepting writes.

Saving
Sum across all qualifying rows once Part 1 is fixed. Individually small, but zero-risk and quick to implement.

