APPENDIX B — Utilisation metrics for a shortlist
Run in Cloud Shell (PowerShell). Replace the list with the databases you intend to change.

powershell
$targets = @(
  @{rg="c190voargpbstlasit"; server="bstsitlaserver"; db="bstsitlarep"},
  @{rg="c190voargpvosdevdatasyncndr"; server="vos-iaz-sql-dev-datasyncs"; db="vosiazsqldbdevndrdatasyncR2"}
)
$start = (Get-Date).AddDays(-30).ToString("yyyy-MM-ddTHH:mm:ssZ")
$out = foreach ($t in $targets) {
  $id = az sql db show -g $t.rg -s $t.server -n $t.db --query id -o tsv
  $metrics = "cpu_percent","app_cpu_billed","dtu_consumption_percent","connection_successful"
  foreach ($m in $metrics) {
    $r = az monitor metrics list --resource $id --metric $m `
         --interval P1D --aggregation Average Maximum Total `
         --start-time $start -o json 2>$null | ConvertFrom-Json
    $d = $r.value.timeseries.data
    [pscustomobject]@{
      database = "$($t.server) / $($t.db)"
      metric   = $m
      avg      = [math]::Round(($d.average | Measure-Object -Average).Average, 2)
      max      = [math]::Round(($d.maximum | Measure-Object -Maximum).Maximum, 2)
      total    = [math]::Round(($d.total   | Measure-Object -Sum).Sum, 2)
    }
  }
}
$out | Export-Csv utilisation.csv -NoTypeInformation
Metrics that don't apply to a database's model return blank — that's expected.

